{"surface": "inspector", "title": "Shock to S&P 500", "html": "<header class=\"hero\"><p class=\"kicker\">Shock</p><h2 class=\"title\"><a class=\"go name\" data-go=\"factor:1\">S&amp;P 500</a></h2><p class=\"ctx\"><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"prop:4\">China blockades or attacks Taiwan by May 18, 2027</a></p></header><h3 class=\"sub\">Whole move</h3><div class=\"sz\"><div class=\"sz-row st\"><div class=\"sz-lab\"><span class=\"sz-t\">Shock</span><span class=\"sz-s\" title=\"Yes\">Yes</span></div><div class=\"po-track\"><i class=\"po-zero\" style=\"left:100.000%\"></i><i class=\"sz-seg st\" style=\"left:5.660%;right:calc(100% - 100.000%)\"></i></div><div class=\"sz-v\"><span class=\"n v\">−17.00%</span></div></div><div class=\"sz-row pw\"><div class=\"sz-lab\"><span class=\"sz-t\">Apr 2 – 8, 2025</span></div><div class=\"po-track\"><i class=\"po-zero\" style=\"left:100.000%\"></i><i class=\"sz-seg pw\" style=\"left:33.003%;right:calc(100% - 100.000%)\"></i></div><div class=\"sz-v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:window:link:106:0\"><span class=\"n v\">−12.07%</span></a></div></div></div><h3 class=\"sub\">Basis</h3><div class=\"basis\"><p class=\"src\"><a class=\"go\" data-go=\"src:211\">taiwannews.com.tw</a></p><blockquote class=\"q\" data-k=\"q0\"><a class=\"go quote\" data-go=\"x:passage:src:211:3ea0c3911f7e\">Even a blockade short of invasion would cut global GDP 5.3% and Taiwan’s 12.5%, Bloomberg projected, as chip inventories dwindle within weeks and production halts in dependent industries.</a></blockquote></div><div class=\"basis note\"><div class=\"fold\"><div class=\"fold-in\"><div class=\"md\" data-md=\"Bloomberg Economics puts a blockade short of invasion at 5.3% of global GDP, with chip inventories gone within weeks. The April 2025 tariff shock, a trade disruption far smaller than cutting off the island that makes most advanced chips, took the S&amp;P down 12% in four sessions (window). I put a blockade-or-attack world 17% below the baseline, weighted toward blockade, with invasion worse.\"><p>Bloomberg Economics puts a blockade short of invasion at 5.3% of global GDP, with chip inventories gone within weeks. The April 2025 tariff shock, a trade disruption far smaller than cutting off the island that makes most advanced chips, took the S&amp;P down 12% in four sessions (window). I put a blockade-or-attack world 17% below the baseline, weighted toward blockade, with invasion worse.</p></div></div><button class=\"linkish more\" type=\"button\" data-more>Show more</button></div></div><h3 class=\"sub\">Levels</h3><table class=\"cmp lv\"><thead><tr><th></th><th class=\"n\">SPY</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Today</th><td class=\"n\"><span class=\"n v\">$715.01</span></td></tr><tr><th>No <span class=\"otag\">Baseline</span></th><td class=\"n\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:level:link:106\"><span class=\"n v\">$719.40</span></a></td></tr><tr><th>Yes</th><td class=\"n\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:level:link:106\"><span class=\"n v\">$597.10</span></a></td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"raw\"><a class=\"rawlink\" data-go=\"raw:value:consequence:link:106\">Full details</a></p>", "wide": true}